WEBVTT

00:26.640 --> 00:27.410
Asuka

00:31.240 --> 00:34.200
Asuka
Incoming call

00:34.500 --> 00:36.080
Drop everything.

00:36.410 --> 00:37.660
We're going...

00:37.660 --> 00:39.500
to the beach!

00:41.250 --> 00:43.660
That was your "very important" issue?

00:43.660 --> 00:45.040
Why now?

00:45.040 --> 00:47.290
It's practically winter.

00:47.750 --> 00:50.660
Well, when I went to put my
summer uniform in my closet,

00:50.660 --> 00:54.660
I realized I'd never had a chance to
wear the swimsuit I bought this year!

00:54.870 --> 00:59.160
That reminds me, we planned on going
to the beach over summer break.

00:59.160 --> 01:03.160
But Asuka came down with a really bad cold
and it all fell through.

01:03.290 --> 01:09.120
You're always so energetic and lively, but you've
always gotten sick whenever we go on trips and stuff.

01:09.290 --> 01:12.620
Well, I was pretty clear about not wanting to go.

01:13.790 --> 01:17.370
Those reasons are exactly why
I wanna go to the beach!

01:17.370 --> 01:19.660
Let's all go have some fun!

01:19.660 --> 01:22.500
Look, I'm already wearing my suit!

01:22.620 --> 01:24.250
Ugh, you must be so sweaty.

01:24.250 --> 01:26.200
Yup, it's pretty muggy under this jacket.

01:26.200 --> 01:29.500
So c'mon, let's go, let's goooo!

01:29.500 --> 01:32.160
I'd go if it were a little warmer.

01:32.160 --> 01:34.580
I'd go if it were a little sunnier.

01:34.580 --> 01:36.660
I'd go if I didn't have cram school.

01:37.620 --> 01:42.040
I'll go as long as I get some time to myself.

01:42.290 --> 01:46.910
I know a place where
all of those wishes will come true!

01:46.910 --> 01:48.290
Sexy Yu-chan?!

01:49.000 --> 01:50.200
You again?!

01:52.830 --> 01:53.700
Hey!

01:54.040 --> 01:58.040
You don't have to wait till 4:44, you can just use this!

01:58.040 --> 01:59.290
Cool tip, huh?

01:59.660 --> 02:00.790
Huh?!

03:41.870 --> 03:46.750
C'mon, everyone, jump in!

03:47.450 --> 03:49.660
We would, but...

03:49.660 --> 03:52.000
We don't have our swimsuits.

03:52.000 --> 03:55.200
You should've explained things a little more in detail...

03:55.200 --> 03:57.250
before we did the stupid ceremony!

03:58.160 --> 04:00.080
Okay, all set.

04:00.370 --> 04:03.000
Now you just have to do your usual thing.

04:03.000 --> 04:06.000
You're fine with being the link this time, right, Chloe?

04:06.000 --> 04:09.160
I just want to be able to spend some time by myself.

04:09.160 --> 04:13.540
Just to make sure, you really didn't
detect any Clutters there, right?

04:13.750 --> 04:18.160
Please, I wouldn't take you to a world
where Boring Asuka might come and visit.

04:18.160 --> 04:19.290
Don't worry!

04:19.290 --> 04:21.120
Okay, let's go!

04:21.290 --> 04:23.080
A Fragment...

04:23.080 --> 04:25.000
of eternal summer!

04:25.000 --> 04:28.830
Whoa. Is it just me,
or have your boobs gotten bigger?

04:30.040 --> 04:33.330
You've got a good eye, Tounaka-kun!

04:33.700 --> 04:35.660
That top is totally squishing them together.

04:35.660 --> 04:36.830
It is not!

04:36.830 --> 04:41.250
My mom says it's not healthy to squeeze or push
your breasts up too much when you're still growing.

04:41.250 --> 04:43.160
That's not it, though!

04:43.160 --> 04:45.160
Why are you guys always...

04:46.950 --> 04:49.450
Brrr! C'mon, Chloe, let's go already!

04:50.540 --> 04:52.000
O-okay.

04:55.540 --> 04:59.700
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight!

05:13.910 --> 05:18.500
You never told us the sacred tree
was underwater here!

05:18.500 --> 05:22.620
I did tell you this Fragment is just one big ocean.

05:22.620 --> 05:24.950
Yeah, but that doesn't mean...

05:24.950 --> 05:26.950
Wait! What...

05:27.290 --> 05:28.580
That's way too skimpy!

05:29.620 --> 05:31.410
Oh, this?

05:31.950 --> 05:34.950
You jealous?
You can wear one just like it, you know.

05:34.950 --> 05:36.160
I'm not going to!

05:36.160 --> 05:39.750
It's so unfair that you have a swimsuit, Sexy Yu-chan!

05:39.910 --> 05:45.410
I travel through lots of Fragments,
so I've got to be ready for any situation.

05:45.410 --> 05:47.040
Don't worry, though!

05:47.290 --> 05:51.370
I ordered some swimsuits for you guys, too,
with this capriphone.

05:51.580 --> 05:52.580
Huh?

05:52.580 --> 05:53.910
Look, look!

05:53.910 --> 05:56.040
Something weird's flying this way!

05:57.750 --> 06:00.160
You have a package from White Goat.

06:00.160 --> 06:01.620
Thanks!

06:06.000 --> 06:08.830
Come forth, my exposed self!

06:09.660 --> 06:11.370
Duplicate!

06:12.160 --> 06:15.410
Look! The water's so clear!

06:37.370 --> 06:40.660
That's right. I'm the link.

06:41.830 --> 06:43.700
That means...

06:44.540 --> 06:47.370
This is where I live in this world.

06:49.290 --> 06:53.830
A Fragment where everyone gets their own little island...

06:54.410 --> 06:56.370
It's a bit strange...

06:56.370 --> 07:00.950
but perfect for someone like me.

07:05.500 --> 07:09.830
So White Goat is the name of this community's AI.

07:10.120 --> 07:13.870
In this world, each community has its own AI

07:13.870 --> 07:17.870
that manages and distributes
everything you need to live your life.

07:17.870 --> 07:19.040
So...

07:19.450 --> 07:21.950
You have a package from White Goat.

07:23.290 --> 07:26.200
See? Anything you order comes right away.

07:26.200 --> 07:29.580
Here's everything we need for a barbecue!

07:30.040 --> 07:33.290
Let's grill it up!

07:34.160 --> 07:37.370
Also included in this delivery
are capriphones for all of your guests.

07:37.370 --> 07:39.500
This service is included free of charge.

07:39.500 --> 07:41.500
Oh, that was thoughtful of you.

07:41.790 --> 07:44.500
If you need something, do not hesitate to call.

07:45.580 --> 07:47.200
I get it.

07:47.910 --> 07:50.700
But doesn't this island belong to someone?

07:50.700 --> 07:52.580
Is it cool for us to be here like this?

07:52.580 --> 07:58.120
Oh, this island belongs to the me,
and you, from this world.

07:58.120 --> 07:58.950
What?

07:58.950 --> 08:04.250
But she's gone missing here for some reason,
so I borrowed her capriphone.

08:04.250 --> 08:07.040
She'll pay for everything we order!

08:08.410 --> 08:09.660
That's straight-up robbery!

08:09.660 --> 08:12.500
How can I be robbing from myself?

08:12.500 --> 08:17.250
Hold on, forget that, what's happened
to my double in this world?

08:17.250 --> 08:19.660
Who cares about those stuffy details?

08:19.660 --> 08:22.200
C'mon, try ordering something.

08:22.200 --> 08:26.120
Anything you want comes right away.
It's pretty addictive!

08:26.120 --> 08:29.950
For example, you can order clothes,
try them on, then return them.

08:31.290 --> 08:33.540
It has games, too!

08:33.540 --> 08:37.040
Oh, it looks like you can get
a rare character in the current event!

08:34.110 --> 08:37.110
3 Million Downloads!
Get a rare character
in our thank-you event!

08:37.250 --> 08:38.700
Look, look!

08:39.370 --> 08:41.910
This picture came out perfect!

08:41.910 --> 08:45.160
And look at all these Nices!
They just keep pouring in!

08:45.500 --> 08:51.290
If White Goat approves of an image,
it gets shared with the whole world.

08:51.290 --> 08:54.580
It's pretty rare that it does. That's amazing!

08:54.580 --> 08:58.160
Ohmigosh! I'm gonna have fans all over the world!

09:09.910 --> 09:12.250
They're looking pretty good!

09:13.750 --> 09:17.500
It looks like you can buy things with this device.

09:17.830 --> 09:19.950
I don't need anything right now, though.

09:27.660 --> 09:31.540
Her taste in books and music is the same as mine.

09:31.540 --> 09:33.540
Guess it's just in our blood.

09:38.750 --> 09:40.620
I'm so full!

09:40.620 --> 09:43.200
I wish Chloe would've come with us.

09:43.200 --> 09:44.790
Should we give her a call?

09:45.080 --> 09:48.040
Some people have much more fun by themselves.

09:48.040 --> 09:50.830
A freakishly outgoing girl like you
probably wouldn't understand.

09:50.830 --> 09:53.830
There you go, pretending you're
the only one who gets it.

09:53.830 --> 09:57.540
Seriously! It's so annoying how she does that, huh?

09:57.540 --> 09:58.750
I know!

09:58.750 --> 10:00.700
Make fun of me all you want, Asuka,

10:00.700 --> 10:03.040
but I don't want to hear that from you!

10:03.450 --> 10:07.870
Now that you mention it, Chloe-senpai
doesn't hang out with us much on weekends,

10:07.870 --> 10:11.040
she usually spends the whole day out somewhere.

10:11.870 --> 10:14.790
It definitely feels like there's
something different about her.

10:15.120 --> 10:18.750
I mean, I just chalked it up to her
growing up outside Japan.

10:18.750 --> 10:20.120
France, right?

10:20.120 --> 10:26.700
Compared to a collectivist society like Japan,
Europe has a lot of people who are very independent.

10:27.000 --> 10:29.000
Maybe she feels uncomfortable.

10:29.950 --> 10:32.660
But we're not telling her to be like us or anything!

10:32.660 --> 10:35.660
We just like hanging out with her,
so we're inviting her over!

10:35.870 --> 10:37.160
Oh, I got it!

10:38.580 --> 10:39.500
Hey!

10:40.250 --> 10:42.250
Can we text Chloe?

10:42.250 --> 10:44.950
I bet we could send her something
with these things, right?

10:45.500 --> 10:48.040
I mean, we could send her something...

10:48.040 --> 10:49.790
But it's kind of annoying.

10:53.830 --> 10:55.910
That was a great book.

10:57.410 --> 11:00.750
Alone time really is the best.

11:00.950 --> 11:03.330
Okay, what to read next...

11:07.620 --> 11:09.830
A programming book?

11:09.830 --> 11:12.950
Guess there are some hobbies
we don't have in common.

11:14.250 --> 11:16.870
VR? That could be cool!

11:23.370 --> 11:28.160
"Don't think, entrust yourself to us."

11:29.200 --> 11:31.330
Is that a quote from something?

11:31.330 --> 11:34.040
I don't think I'd be into a quote like that, though...

11:39.830 --> 11:41.830
You've got mail. You've got mail.

11:41.830 --> 11:42.750
Huh?!

11:43.950 --> 11:46.540
Mail? Like physical mail?

11:48.940 --> 11:51.910
To Chloe
From Asuka

11:53.830 --> 11:56.000
This is so cute!

11:56.370 --> 12:00.200
I was just going to try it on, but I think I'll buy it!

12:00.540 --> 12:05.120
You sure? It's gonna be this world's Yu
who has to pay for it.

12:05.120 --> 12:08.790
Well, it's my capriphone.
What's wrong with me using it?

12:08.790 --> 12:09.950
Whaaa...

12:09.950 --> 12:11.950
You've got mail. You've got mail.

12:11.950 --> 12:13.830
Ooh, a reply from Chloe!

12:13.830 --> 12:15.540
This world is so weird.

12:15.540 --> 12:19.500
You've got such an incredible network,
but you can't send electronic mail.

12:19.790 --> 12:22.500
You've gotta write it out and
have a drone deliver it for you.

12:22.500 --> 12:23.950
What a pain!

12:24.160 --> 12:28.160
But it feels so much more personal
than a text message.

12:28.410 --> 12:30.950
What did she write to us?

12:30.950 --> 12:32.910
"Thanks for the letter."

12:33.200 --> 12:36.750
"I'm having a good time by myself. No need to worry."

12:36.750 --> 12:41.120
"We'll meet up tomorrow when it's time to go back."

12:41.120 --> 12:42.370
No surprises there.

12:42.750 --> 12:46.160
She said she's fine, so let's leave her alone.

12:46.160 --> 12:48.660
If she changes her mind, she'll let us know.

12:49.080 --> 12:50.250
Okay...

12:53.200 --> 12:56.910
"Somewhat Lonely" Asuka is sooo adorable!

12:57.750 --> 12:59.160
I knew it.

13:03.250 --> 13:05.500
Oh, you're here.

13:10.620 --> 13:13.700
Ooh, why're you taking me all the way out here?

13:13.700 --> 13:16.450
Do you wanna make out with me or something?

13:16.660 --> 13:18.290
What is the meaning of this?

13:18.290 --> 13:21.910
Why did you take those girls to
another Fragment for no good reason?

13:21.910 --> 13:24.370
Oh, I had a good reason!

13:24.370 --> 13:27.370
I just wanted to make Asuka happy!

13:27.660 --> 13:31.040
Oh, not you, the cute Asuka.

13:31.040 --> 13:35.790
I didn't detect any Clutters in this world.
What's wrong with staying one night?

13:35.790 --> 13:37.830
Don't use that girl as an excuse.

13:38.120 --> 13:41.540
Everything you do is driven by
your own selfish desires.

13:42.870 --> 13:44.160
Really?

13:44.160 --> 13:50.160
What about when you ignored those girls
and their duel to go through with your own plans?

13:50.450 --> 13:53.410
My plans wouldn't cause any trouble.

13:53.410 --> 13:56.200
More importantly, those plans
were to take out Clutters.

13:56.450 --> 14:00.870
Which you're just doing
to save your own Fragment, right?

14:01.200 --> 14:03.580
Wouldn't you say that's pretty selfish?

14:05.910 --> 14:09.250
I've met a lot of Asukas in my time.

14:09.250 --> 14:13.290
Every Fragments' Asuka is different.

14:13.290 --> 14:18.000
I've met the cute Asukas I'm really into,
and Asukas who aren't that cute...

14:18.000 --> 14:21.370
But I've never met an Asuka
who's as big of a hypocrite as you are!

14:24.660 --> 14:26.750
You really piss me off...

14:33.200 --> 14:36.580
...just like the person who
stole Asuka away from me!

14:36.750 --> 14:38.450
Come forth, my twilight self!

14:43.000 --> 14:44.830
Duplicate!

14:47.080 --> 14:48.580
That's right.

14:48.830 --> 14:51.580
See if you can use brute force to shut me up!

14:55.910 --> 14:57.200
Don't underestimate me!

15:06.370 --> 15:07.870
What're you doing?!

15:11.660 --> 15:14.910
Oh, Asuka! This is no big deal.

15:14.910 --> 15:18.790
See, I flipped up her skirt,
and she just lost it on me!

15:18.790 --> 15:21.000
This is just a little scuffle, that's all!

15:21.290 --> 15:23.080
Her skirt?

15:23.500 --> 15:25.330
Yup, her skirt.

15:26.950 --> 15:28.160
Hey, Asuka?

15:28.160 --> 15:29.160
What?

15:30.250 --> 15:31.620
Go get 'er.

15:34.700 --> 15:36.660
What? Hey!

15:37.790 --> 15:39.080
Just kidding!

15:46.910 --> 15:50.160
So that's why I'm giving her another new nickname!

15:50.160 --> 15:53.580
Say hello to Seriouska, Burglasuka,

15:53.580 --> 15:55.540
and now, Angryska!

15:55.540 --> 15:57.410
C-could you stop already?

15:57.410 --> 15:59.660
Oh, hey, Asuka-chan.

15:59.660 --> 16:03.040
There are drinks over there if you're thirsty.

16:03.040 --> 16:04.750
We've got chips, too.

16:04.750 --> 16:06.080
No reaction...

16:06.290 --> 16:08.580
Guess "Angryska" isn't very funny.

16:08.790 --> 16:12.870
Well, the only one that really works
as a pun is Seriouska.

16:12.870 --> 16:15.330
It's been dead since Burglasuka.

16:15.330 --> 16:16.410
So strict!

16:21.120 --> 16:22.450
This is boring.

16:26.080 --> 16:28.700
Wonder if there's anything good...

16:40.500 --> 16:43.040
Huh? Why is it Christmas?

16:43.040 --> 16:45.330
Sorry, did I make you wait?

16:45.830 --> 16:48.080
You're so cute today, Chloe-chan.

16:48.080 --> 16:49.500
Wh-what is this?!

16:49.830 --> 16:50.830
Hey.

16:54.120 --> 16:59.330
I hope to God my double's not a fan of that guy.

17:00.870 --> 17:04.830
Man, who knew you'd come here too, Asuka?

17:05.080 --> 17:08.370
But if you're here without detecting any Clutters...

17:08.370 --> 17:10.580
I didn't come because I was worried about you or-

17:10.580 --> 17:13.200
You came because you wanted to go to the beach!

17:14.160 --> 17:16.080
Sure, that's it.

17:18.040 --> 17:20.330
It's so nice, isn't it?

17:20.330 --> 17:23.910
The roaring waves, the leaves rustling in the breeze,

17:24.200 --> 17:27.830
the birds chirping, it's all so relaxing...

17:29.000 --> 17:30.910
Yeah.

17:31.870 --> 17:36.040
It's full of color, life, and change.

17:37.700 --> 17:41.080
The compete opposite of the World of Twilight.

17:42.450 --> 17:46.080
Is that what the World of Twilight is like?

17:46.410 --> 17:51.500
Yeah. Nothing dies, and nothing is born.

17:51.950 --> 17:54.950
There's no pain, but there's no happiness, either.

17:54.950 --> 18:00.250
It's an endless world where all possibilities
have been lost, and life has come to a stop.

18:00.870 --> 18:04.200
That's what the King of Twilight brings to worlds.

18:08.370 --> 18:10.790
It sounds awful.

18:11.250 --> 18:13.580
Yeah. It is.

18:15.080 --> 18:17.120
I've got to cleanse my palate...

18:16.750 --> 18:17.870
Worldwide Walks: Paris

18:18.080 --> 18:21.080
Paris! I haven't been back in forever.

18:26.450 --> 18:28.660
This is bringing back so many memories!

18:30.450 --> 18:34.830
Back then, I was always on my own...

18:37.040 --> 18:40.950
But I never felt sad or alone.

18:42.000 --> 18:46.620
Every day, there were so many things
to see, to hear, to imagine.

18:49.000 --> 18:52.750
Being on my own was always such a treat.

18:54.500 --> 18:57.000
But after I moved to Japan...

18:57.000 --> 19:00.830
Everyone told me that it was sad to be alone.

19:01.500 --> 19:04.450
Even though I didn't think it was...

19:04.750 --> 19:08.250
I started feeling that way, too.

19:09.410 --> 19:12.700
I have a lot of fun with everyone
in the Radio Research Society.

19:12.700 --> 19:14.000
But...

19:14.540 --> 19:16.750
Sometimes, I worry.

19:17.700 --> 19:20.790
If I get too accustomed to being around everyone,

19:21.160 --> 19:25.370
will I start to feel afraid to be alone?

19:26.450 --> 19:30.450
That's why sometimes, I want to be alone.

19:31.500 --> 19:34.370
I feel like I have to be alone.

19:40.910 --> 19:42.540
I should stop.

19:42.870 --> 19:46.290
This is getting me too emotional.

19:47.790 --> 19:50.580
Huh? Those symbols.

20:02.120 --> 20:06.080
"Don't think, entrust yourself to us."

20:13.830 --> 20:15.120
I finished!

20:15.120 --> 20:16.540
Let's take a look.

20:17.750 --> 20:20.290
"Dear Chloe, are you having a good time?"

20:20.660 --> 20:23.120
"Did you eat something yummy?"

20:23.120 --> 20:27.500
"If you're hungry, I'll send you some chikuwa."

20:29.620 --> 20:32.250
Sounds like you're the hungry one.

20:32.250 --> 20:36.450
I can't help it! It's been a while since we had lunch!

20:36.450 --> 20:38.790
That barbecue was soooo good.

20:40.160 --> 20:44.250
Well, well, sounds like your body's
much more honest than you are, madam!

20:44.250 --> 20:45.500
Sh-shut up!

20:45.500 --> 20:49.250
After I send this letter, let's have an early dinner!

20:51.080 --> 20:53.330
Hey guys, are you hungry?

20:53.330 --> 20:55.160
I dunno...

20:55.160 --> 20:57.080
Let's make dinner!

20:57.080 --> 21:00.160
Why, though? We don't have to.

21:00.160 --> 21:02.370
I'll just eat chips.

21:02.370 --> 21:05.750
Ooh, I'm getting more Nices! Yay!

21:05.750 --> 21:07.160
Aww...

21:07.160 --> 21:09.620
I'll help you with dinner.

21:09.910 --> 21:12.450
I bet once you serve dinner, they'll all eat it.

21:12.450 --> 21:14.540
Yeah, you're right.

21:15.580 --> 21:17.250
By the way, I brought something with me.

21:17.620 --> 21:18.750
Your family's miso.

21:18.750 --> 21:22.580
Really?! Yay, let's make miso soup!

21:32.790 --> 21:35.080
What the hell is this...

21:37.700 --> 21:39.410
It's not just the VR...

21:39.750 --> 21:41.410
It's in the shopping app,

21:41.660 --> 21:43.290
the gaming apps,

21:43.450 --> 21:45.290
and the camera apps...

21:45.500 --> 21:47.910
They all have those symbols...

21:59.110 --> 22:01.070
Subliminal?

21:59.540 --> 22:03.040
There's something very wrong with this world!

22:01.070 --> 22:03.040
Brainwashing?
